Subject: [PATCH] Untrack stale maps when the kernel returns a non-fixed mapping

Cosmopolitan 4.0.2 estimates the main stack from RLIMIT_STACK and tracks an
additional 1 MiB guard below it. On macOS arm64, raising the soft stack limit
can put that estimated guard outside the kernel's actual stack reservation.
CMake raises this limit to the hard limit at startup on macOS.

The kernel can return non-fixed mappings inside this estimated guard.
Inserting them without removing stale tracking entries creates overlapping
maps. A later munmap() can then partially overlap more than two entries,
violating __muntrack()'s bound and overrunning __munmap()'s Map temp[2].

Untrack the returned range before inserting every successful non-Windows
mapping, as fixed mappings already do. Windows keeps its reservation path.

TODO: [external] Drop this downstream patch after an upstream fix is released.
TODO: Add the upstream issue/reproducer link once published.
---
 libc/intrin/mmap.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libc/intrin/mmap.c b/libc/intrin/mmap.c
--- a/libc/intrin/mmap.c
+++ b/libc/intrin/mmap.c
@@ -851,9 +851,12 @@ static void *__mmap_impl(char *addr, size_t size, int prot, int flags, int fd,
   if (!IsWindows()) {
     struct Map *deleted = 0;
     __maps_lock();
-    if (fixedmode)
-      if (__muntrack(res.addr, size, &deleted, 0, 0))
-        STRACE("memtrack compromised by hole punch oom");
+    // keep tracking consistent with the kernel, including non-fixed maps
+    // that overlap an inaccurately estimated main-stack guard. overlapping
+    // entries can overflow the two-element scratch array that __munmap()
+    // passes to __muntrack()
+    if (__muntrack(res.addr, size, &deleted, 0, 0))
+      STRACE("memtrack compromised by hole punch oom");
     __maps_insert(map);
     __maps_unlock();
     __maps_free_all(deleted);
